every window within the window js file starts off the same way - by inheriting from some other window. So if more examples are needed, theyre all there
Code:
function Window_CustomHelp() {
    this.initialize(...arguments);
}

Window_CustomHelp.prototype = Object.create(Window_Help.prototype);
Window_CustomHelp.prototype.constructor = Window_CustomHelp;
that defines a new window thats just a copy of WIndow_Help, but called Window_CustomHelp.
now any change you made prior to Window_Help can be moved to this one instead. then from there, youd look in the scenes js file, look at the functions that creates the help windows for skill and item scene, and change them from making a new Window_Help to a new Window_CustomHelp (within the plugin, not the scenes file).
now those two scenes use your altered help window and all the others ones like the equip scene are untouched

